                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "18445616",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198027483587",
                            "num_reviews": 282,
                            "playtime_forever": 122,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 119,
                            "last_played": 1444681382
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I say this pretty often, but this game is another argument for the need for a \"neutral\" option on steam reviews, instead of just YES or NO. View this as a tentative YES, leaning heavily towards NO for the state it's in right now. This game needs work. A lot of work. Also- some of the positive reviews are really fishy. First-time reviewers who are overly enthusiastic about a game they have .1 hours in. It reeks of friends + family reviews. One of them even has 'MUMMY' in their name. Review continues below: \n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-yrVYc8kMVY\n\nThe concept here is fantastic. It's sort of a blend of 'Battleblock Theater' and 'Mighty Quest For Epic Loot'. Build your 'pyramid' using blocks, traps, etc- to try to prevent other players from making it to the end and stealing your treasure. Similarly, of course- you try to defeat other players'. \n\nThere is a cash shop. I'm holding off judgement on that for now, to see how necessary it seems... but for now, just know that there are seemingly only a small handful of items you can use in your Pyramid without having currency. It's DEFINITELY early access. There are some big issues. I can't get my xbox one controller to work with the game at all. Often at the start of a level, the game just repeatedly kills the character every second until you reset the game. It's often choppy. It definitely has promise, and there's some fun to be had even in this state.",
